      "sentences": [
        { "caption": "Tagway doesn't want *Glide*. | They want their own image loading library. | And your job is to *build* it." },
        { "caption": "It takes *five layers*. | And every layer fixes a *problem*." },
        { "caption": "You start simple:#naive | for every row, download the image, | decode a new bitmap, | and show it." },
        { "caption": "QA tests it:#qa | \"I scrolled fast. | The scroll *stutters*.#crash | Then the app *crashes*.\"" },
        { "caption": "Here's why. | Every new image allocates new *memory*, | and old bitmaps become garbage." },
        { "caption": "So garbage collection#gcbig runs again and again, | and every pause steals *frames* from your scroll." },
        { "caption": "So you add a *bitmap pool*.#pool | Like washing plates instead of buying new ones." },
        { "caption": "When a row scrolls off,#rowoff | its bitmap goes back to the pool,#topool | and the next image#nextimg is decoded | into that *same memory*.#same" },
        { "caption": "\"No new memory. | Fewer GC pauses. | *Smooth*#smooth scroll.\"" },
        { "caption": "Then the product manager#pm says, | \"Our gallery has a *thousand* images. | Users jump straight to the last one.\"" },
        { "caption": "At one megabyte per second, | with one megabyte per image, | that's a *thousand seconds*#wait of waiting." },
        { "caption": "So you add *task management*.#task | Every request is tied to its view. | When a view leaves the screen, | its download is *cancelled*.#cancel" },
        { "caption": "The network is free, | and only *visible* images download." },
        { "caption": "\"The last image loads | in about a *second*.\"#fast" },
        { "caption": "Then crash reports#oom come in: | \"*OutOfMemoryError*.\"" },
        {
          "caption": "A photo is *1000px x 1000px*, | but the ImageView is only *200px x 200px*.",
          "say": "A photo is a thousand by a thousand pixels, but the ImageView is only two hundred by two hundred."
        },
        {
          "caption": "At four bytes per pixel, | the full photo#fourmb needs *4MB* of memory.",
          "say": "At four bytes per pixel, the full photo needs four megabytes of memory."
        },
        { "caption": "So you add *downsampling*.#down | Decode the image at the size of the view." },
        {
          "caption": "200px x 200px needs#small only *160KB*. | *25x less*.",
          "say": "Two hundred by two hundred needs only a hundred and sixty kilobytes. Twenty-five times less."
        },
        { "caption": "\"No more *crashes*.\"" },
        { "caption": "Then a user scrolls back up,#back | and every image downloads *again*.#again" },
        { "caption": "So you add a *memory cache*,#mem | in RAM.#ram | The fastest place to read from." },
        { "caption": "\"Scrolling back is *instant*.\"#instant" },
        { "caption": "Then the user closes the app#reopen | and opens it again." },
        { "caption": "RAM is *wiped*,#wiped | and every image downloads again." },
        { "caption": "So you add a *disk cache*.#disk | It survives restarts." },
        { "caption": "Now every request checks RAM#chkram first, | then disk,#chkdisk | and only then the network.#chknet | And every downloaded image is saved to *both*.#both" },
        { "caption": "\"No second *download*.\"#nosecond" },
        { "caption": "So the full flow#full is: | download,#f1 downsample,#f2 | cache,#f3 and display.#f4" },
        { "caption": "After weeks#weeks of work, | Tagway's library is smooth,#b1 fast,#b2 | and *memory-safe*.#b3" },
        { "caption": "Then one day, | someone wants sharper images, | and loads every photo at its *original size*.#orig" },
        { "caption": "QA scrolls fast.#qa2" },
        { "caption": "\"The scroll *stutters*.#crash2 | Then the app crashes.\"" }
      ]
    },
